-+++
-+++streamplan.h has computed a status and two lines every pass since 0200
-+++and nothing has ever drawn them. The reason turned out to be duller than
-+++the open list implied: s_stream_top and s_stream_bottom were declared
-+++beside play_stream(), four thousand lines below ui_task, so in one
-+++translation unit ui_task could not name them. "Read by nothing" was
-+++enforced by declaration order. They move up beside s_streaming, which
-+++was moved for this exact reason when it was added.
-+++
-+++ui_state_t gains three fields:
-+++
-+++  live           this is a stream, so there is no position
-+++  stream_status  "Connecting" / "Buffering" / "Reconnecting" / "No
-+++                 signal", or "" when there is nothing to say
-+++  stream_title   the ICY title, or empty
-+++
-+++`live` is its own flag and not "len_sec == 0", because those mean
-+++opposite things. An unknown duration is a gap in what the player knows
-+++and the bar says so -- bare groove, both clocks dashed. A live stream is
-+++not missing a position; it does not have one. Drawing the
-+++unknown-duration state for it reports a fault where there is none, which
-+++is what the board has been showing for eight patches.
-+++
-+++So row 2 becomes a filled LIVE pill with the status beside it on one
-+++baseline, in the band the envelope would have stood in -- the row a
-+++stream cancels is the row that has to explain itself, and left empty it
-+++is a 72 px hole that reads as something not yet loaded. Row 3 goes blank
-+++rather than dashed, for the same reason. The ICY title takes the album
-+++row, keeping the order streamplan_lines() already chose: the station is
-+++what was chosen and stays, the title changes underneath it.
-+++
-+++The status arrives as a string through streamplan_status_text() rather
-+++than as the enum. It is a function of netstream's state AND the buffer
-+++phase, those two disagree deliberately, and streamplan.h holds the table
-+++and the host test for reconciling them; handing ui.c the enum would put
-+++that reasoning in a draw call.
-+++
-+++Both gates in ui_draw() are one-line extensions of existing `if`s, so
-+++the 130 lines of seek and clock logic are untouched and unreindented.
-+++Nothing is a new hit target: ui_touch() already gates the seek drag on
-+++can_seek, which is false for the life of a stream.
-+++
-+++Depends on the previous patch, which is what empties the artist and album
-+++rows -- without it this draws the ICY title under the last file's album.
-+++
-+++Not flashed. ui.c compiles clean at -O2 -Werror against the texttest
-+++fakes, which checks the arithmetic and nothing about how it looks.
-+++
-+++Three things deliberately not done, each its own decision:
-+++  - "No signal" is terminal and the other three states are not, and all
-+++    four are drawn the same. The difference is worth drawing and cannot
-+++    be recovered from a string; it needs its own flag.
-+++  - No elapsed counter. Time-connected is a real number, but nothing
-+++    counts it today and a reconnect resetting it is a decision.
-+++  - The marquee stays on the station row, though the ICY title is the
-+++    line most likely to overrun.
