@@ -0,0 +1,7715 @@
+From 332624de79ab800642dfbdeda185f76f1b8a1b46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
+Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:50:06 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] netdec.c -- the stack check was reading the past, not the
+ headroom
+
+0308 cleared the routing noise and left this unambiguous: with the rows
+correct and the station correctly identified, every stream after a file
+has played is refused, and the figure in the message keeps changing --
+5604 after a stream, 2068 after a 256 kbps file.
+
+uxTaskGetStackHighWaterMark() returns the smallest free stack RECORDED
+SINCE THE TASK STARTED, not what is free now. On the main task the
+smallest ever recorded is set by the deepest thing that has run on it,
+and the deepest thing is mp3dec_decode_frame() from play_file(), putting
+its 17744 bytes there. So:
+
+  boot, chooser open, nothing played yet   passes, the stream plays
+  after one file has played                2068, refused for the rest
+                                           of the boot
+
+A high-water mark only ever goes down, so the refusal is permanent, and
+it arrives with a message naming a stack size that was already correct.
+That is why the first station of a boot always worked and every one after
+a file never did.
+
+**2068 IS THE PROOF THE CHECK WAS WRONG.** A task whose worst-ever free
+is 2068 has already survived a 17744-byte minimp3 call -- that call is
+exactly what put the figure there. The measurement was reading the record
+of the demand being met as evidence that it could not be met.
+
+It is the error at the top of CLAUDE.md from the other direction. That
+one says a stack protection fault reports the overshoot rather than the
+demand; this one says a high-water mark reports the past rather than the
+present. Neither of them is the headroom, and both were read as if they
+were.
+
+Headroom is the distance from this frame down to the bottom of the
+task's stack: pxTaskGetStackStart() gives the bottom, the address of a
+local is in this frame, the stack grows down, and the difference is what
+a callee may still use. Current, measured, and unaffected by anything
+that has already returned. The message is reworded to say "below this
+frame", because that is what is now being reported and the old wording
+would be a second thing to disbelieve.
+
+NETDEC_STACK_FLOOR keeps its value and gains a note in netdec.h saying
+what it is compared against and why the mark cannot answer the question.
+
+Not flashed. The test is the one that has failed twice: play a file,
+open RADIO, pick a station.
