+-From 912b1360e1c2838e2c0afa630efd74d832c4745b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+-From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
+-Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:31:36 +0000
+-Subject: [PATCH 307/307] CLAUDE.md -- radio-browser, and why it had never been
+- touched
+-
+-The record for 0306, and an answer to the question that prompted it:
+-radio-browser integration was the headline of v0.4.0 and no line of code
+-mentioned it.
+-
+-The reason is worth keeping rather than apologising for. Everything built
+-so far was scaffolding FOR radio-browser -- stations.m3u is M3U because
+-radio-browser serves M3U, stationlist.h says so in its opening
+-paragraph, netstream does the TLS, the portal does the typing -- and
+-scaffolding described in terms of a thing is easy to mistake for the
+-thing. Four patches of this series went into a station screen without
+-anyone noticing that the station data had no source.
+-
+-The four API facts are recorded because each would otherwise have been
+-learned from a failed flash, and the TLS one would have been learned as
+-an unexplained certificate error three patches into a fetch.
+-
+-One entry is a warning rather than a note, and is placed where it will be
+-read by whoever adds the writing: a stations.m3u built from a search must
+-copy the response body through verbatim rather than being regenerated
+-from parsed stations. Regenerating is the obvious implementation, it
+-discards #RADIOBROWSERUUID, and the loss is invisible -- the stations
+-still play, and the one obligation this service imposes can never be
+-honoured again.
+-
+-The open list is ordered by what unblocks what, and the second entry is
+-the one with real scope in it: there is no way to type a search term, the
+-portal is the only answer, and that means the portal has to be reachable
+-while the player is joined to a network rather than only while it is an
+-AP.
