++From 1a2da4c352e25bf3329aeff823a908fd79a8f11b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
++Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:44:00 +0000
++Subject: [PATCH 308/309] browser.c -- reopening the chooser leaves the radio
++ tab behind
++
++browser_open() sets s_tab in three places and has never touched s_radio.
++select_tab() is the only thing that clears it, and browser_open() does
++not go through select_tab(). So once the RADIO tab had been visited,
++every subsequent open of the chooser drew a volume's files with s_radio
++still true.
++
++The board found it and the log says it plainly:
++
++  button: row 3 (station) "Advent_Chamber_Orchestra_-_04_-_Mozart..."
++  station 4 of 4: ice1.somafm.com
++
++That is a file row, named as a station, playing whichever station sat at
++that index. Rows past the end of a four-entry list played nothing while
++the press logged as received, which is the dead-button shape 0302 was
++about. `radio: 4 stations` was drawn over a nine-file listing, the footer
++offered RLOD over a directory, and UP and FLDR were refused on a
++directory that has both.
++
++Worth noting what it took to see: a station list with entries in it AND a
++station played AND the chooser reopened afterwards. Every earlier flash
++had no stations.m3u, so s_radio had never been true when browser_open()
++ran, and the missing line could not do anything. It has been missing
++since the RADIO tab landed in 0207.
++
++Reset in browser_open() rather than by routing it through select_tab().
++select_tab() loads, and browser_open() has three different ideas about
++what to load and from which volume; folding them together to reach one
++assignment would be a restructure in place of a fix. What was missing was
++one line of state.
++
++Same family as 0301's declaration order and 0302's icon: a mode was
++added to a press and not everything that describes the press was found.
++This is the third instance in the series.
